E={8: '“I smell a waking God made of Mars. Will you sell your mind as a toll fee? Just drink this ignorance…” the shadow speaks.', 12: '“I am a fool’s relation, you could say, and my name is Wisdom of the first of third Limbo,” the shadow speaks.', 16: '“I am the lesson learned, born out of foolishness, and I will answer any questions,” the Wisdom of Limbo speaks.', 20: '“I am the lesson learned after all, so yes,” the Wisdom says.', 28: '“The tree you cut down brings the curse of the joker, whose joke is your loss, and this loss is unforeseen in its dream. The curse will cast your greatest possession into Limbo as bait, and the only way to retrieve it is to become both life and death. Your love could be found within yourself, within the outermost realm of the outer—darkness. This journey either ends in eternal life or death, either togetherness or loneliness. That is how you save the one who is neither living nor dead,” the Wisdom speaks unto the traveler Samson.', 34: '“Me!? Who is the waking God?” Samson seeks to understand this phrase. The taste of blood lingers on his tongue, and the iron will not quit.'}
